# Repository-First Skill Development

- Treat `skills/<skill-name>/` as the only canonical source for every skill.
- Treat `%USERPROFILE%\.cursor\skills\` as an installed runtime/testing copy.
- Never make permanent skill changes in the global runtime directory.
- Create and edit skill files only under this repository's `skills/` directory.
- Deploy repository versions for local testing with `.\install.ps1`.
- When testing fails, fix the repository copy, reinstall, and retest.
- Commit and push to `origin/main` only after testing and QA pass.
- Treat `origin/main` as the latest approved, backed-up, synchronized version.
- On other computers, use `git pull` followed by `.\install.ps1`.
- Never manually synchronize global skill folders when Git is available.
- Keep tokens, client secrets, API keys, passwords, `.env` secrets,
  machine-local authentication, credential directories, caches,
  `__pycache__/`, and `*.pyc` out of Git.
- Keep Excel Google credentials machine-local at
  `%LOCALAPPDATA%\CursorExcelSkill\google\`.

See `WORKFLOW.md` for the complete lifecycle and commands.
